    "body": "fix on issue/983-rings-fallback-note (mkinney fork) · PR #1007 · pinned by machining3d::hsm::fallback_tests (3) and rotary_adaptive::a_microlift_plane_is_not_read_as_an_unnamed_ring_level · merges when reviewed. The radius 5.6 case reproduced on #882's held commit with INSET = 0. It was the test reader counting a microlift's lifted plane (its down ramp has a vertex on 5.6) as a level. It was not a silent planner fallback; every rings arm already named its level. A maintainer please swap `claimed` for `in-review` (labels cannot be edited from the fork).",
